it(W2, "ExecRegressionC1", "executor", """Final no-harm run for C1 on quiescent bytes (poll until {WD}/ExecCBFix.md exists, then run): from {LANE}: `python3 corpus/instruments/capture-binding-check.py` (twice, byte-identical sha256), `python3 corpus/instruments/capture-binding-check.py --selftest`, from `cd /` with `--root {LANE}`, `python3 corpus/instruments/limb-mutation-check.py --ledger corpus/instruments/capture-binding-ledger.json` (twice, stdout byte-identical), the UNCHANGED round-31 `--ledger corpus/instruments/limb-ledger.json` (expect `limbs=13 killed=13 survivors=0`, `controls=3 rejected=3`), `limb-mutation-check.py --selftest`, `python3 corpus/instruments/recheck-audit.py --quiet` (strict pass=45/45 with the F16 entry), `recheck-audit.py --selftest`, `source-recheck.py --selftest`, `python3 corpus/instruments/anchorcheck.py --selftest`, `python3 corpus/instruments/frontier-recheck-count.py` (entries=19 pass=19), `python3 corpus/instruments/claim-package-check.py --selftest`, `python3 corpus/instruments/closure-checks.py --selftest`, and the independent R count (python one-liner in claims.json C1 counter 3) and `with_url` (counter 4). Label every number with its command and exit; paste outputs; compare each with {RD}/c1-controls/before.txt. Verify `git -C {LANE} status --porcelain corpus/` shows no unexpected path. Write {WD}/ExecRegressionC1.md; flag PRE-STATE runs.""")
it(W2, "CritJunkConstruction", "critic", """Reproduce the round-31 junk construction against the NEW instrument (scratch only; recipe in {LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-31/wave1/CritC2Kill.md §4): in a mktemp copy of {LANE}/corpus build (a) an invented capture + manifest + registry row + entry whose URL is a real public page that does NOT contain the invented quote; (b) the same with `url` copied from the registry and a plausible fetched_utc. Run `python3 capture-binding-check.py --root <scratch>` offline (expect PASS on (b) by construction - say so), then run the live-compare against a localhost http.server you start that serves the REAL text at the registry URL's role (you may point the scratch registry row and manifest `url` at 127.0.0.1:<port> to emulate the live page) and show live-absent for the invented quote; then the reverse (honest capture, live page edited) -> live-absent: so live-absent means 'capture and live page disagree', not 'capture is fabricated' (state it). Quantify: how many of the 8 CONTROL lines and which ledger limbs witness each outcome. Verdict: `closes gate caveat 1 for: <exact class>` and `does not close: <exact class>`. Write {WD}/CritJunkConstruction.md.""")
it(W2, "CritCalibration", "critic", """Calibration attack (AXES calibration: self-assessment vs observed state). Read SHONEN.md, SCORECARD.md (round-31 section, Axes, Capabilities, Saturation), corpus/README.md coverage statements, corpus/instruments/README.md, and the landed round-32 bytes. Count mismatches between the lane's self-assessment and observed state with commands: stale live-claim numbers (`grep -n` for registry row counts 48, frontier counts 15, `entries=18`, `strict pass=44/44`, `38 records`, 'F01-F15', '44 entries' in files that should now say 50 / 16 / 19 / 45 / 40; separate historical-by-design lines (append-only R6/R9) from live-claim lines that now read wrong), SHONEN box evidence against the files it cites (does each cited path/command exist and print what the box says: `grep -n` + run), SCORECARD capabilities table vs instruments that exist (`ls corpus/instruments`), PROVINCE frontier list vs README frontier rows (F01-F16), SKILL.md instrument registry vs `ls corpus/instruments/*.py`. Report `mismatches=N` split by (live-wrong / historical-ok / unverifiable) with path:line for each live-wrong one; propose the erratum line, do not edit. Write {WD}/CritCalibration.md.""")

